    "Fontan surgery is associated with prolongation of atrial refractory periods, extensive atrial scarring, and intra-atrial conduction delay. Sinus node dysfunction occurs in up to 45% of adults long-term following Fontan surgery and is linked with reduced single ventricle preload, increased venous pressure, reduced cardiac output, plastic bronchitis, and protein-losing enteropathy. Management may include transvenous atrial pacing or epicardial approach. Electrophysiological management is crucial for atrial tachyarrhythmias, implicated in 60% of adults. Imaging is critical for assessing thrombotic complications and other specific conditions post-surgery.": "These arrhythmias might be poorly tolerated, causing serious hemodynamic compromise. Immediate management strategies are critical, preferably coordinated with specialized care for long-term outcomes."
